ault_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "fb8dcbf3-8908-4fca-9052-bffff65737e7", "reasoning_start_time": 1789413982.6106746, "request_id": "4c5183a3-abaa-427a-81a4-3c47b37bf5ae", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "314af538-a858-47e0-9388-ca8c15e18871", "turn_id": "045b2382-321e-4568-ad85-00bbe2b25859", "working_turn_id": "314af538-a858-47e0-9388-ca8c15e18871"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["I read Talon’s plan. It is **good enough to execute with three Don rulings and two wording corrections**. The core sequencing is right: carry data forward first, verify it, then repoint the shell folders, with no deletion and Luce independently verifying afterward. fileciteturn0file0L19-L30\n\n**Don ruling: APPROVE Priority 1 with these decisions.**\n\n- **D-1 OneDrive: KEEP HELD.** We already know OneDrive is not part of your intended operating model, and Talon verified it is not configured locally. Do not create `%USERPROFILE%\\OneDrive` just to satisfy a stale KnownFolder entry. Leave that entry explicitly documented as unresolved/legacy for now. fileciteturn0file0L58-L61\n- **D-2 Desktop mirrors: DO NOT TOUCH in this run.** `Desktop\\Documents`, `Desktop\\Personal`, `Archive/Archives`, `Audio`, `Images`, `Videos` belong to the broader reconstruction/reconciliation pass after the Windows shell truth is restored. Talon already scoped them out, which is correct. fileciteturn0file0L142-L149\n- **D-3 Kimi occupying Talon: ACCEPTED for this work item.** The seat behavior is correct and the runtime substitution is explicitly disclosed. That is consistent with `MODEL != SEAT`. fileciteturn0file0L150-L150\n\nTwo things I would tighten before Keel runs it. First, the phrase “both HKCU key sets hold identical canonical values” should mean **semantically identical targets**, because `User Shell Folders` should use `%USERPROFILE%` while `Shell Folders` uses expanded absolute paths. They should resolve to the same place, not necessarily contain byte-identical strings. fileciteturn0file0L95-L113\n\nSecond, Talon calls the robocopy mirror a “backup.” It is useful rollback protection, but because it sits on the same machine/drive, I would call it a **local rollback snapshot**, not a real backup. That distinction matters because Proton Drive is currently not syncing. The hash manifest + registry exports + preserved source trees are still sufficient for this local repair pass. fileciteturn0file0L63-L79\n\nThe one procedural tweak I would make: **do not perform an extra experimental Downloads registry flip before the actual run unless Keel has a very specific reason.** The plan already has exported registry rollback, additive copy-forward, and post-change Luce verification. A deliberate flip-and-restore of Downloads adds another mutation to an already messy live profile. If Keel wants to test rollback, do it **after G2 copy-forward and as part of the controlled G1 sequence**, not as a separate exploratory maneuver. The existing rollback design is otherwise sound. fileciteturn0file0L124-L129\n\nSo I would send Talon/Keel this authorization:\n\n> **DON DECISION — APPROVED WITH RULINGS**\n>\n> Proceed with **G2 data carry-forward first, then G1 shell-folder repair**.\n>\n> **D-1:** OneDrive remains HOLD. Do not create or repoint OneDrive in this run.  \n> **D-2:** Desktop mirror/stray folders remain untouched.  \n> **D-3:** Kimi is accepted as temporary Talon occupant for this work item.  \n> **Deletion:** NOT AUTHORIZED.  \n> **GCE hierarchy cleanup:** DEFERRED.  \n> **Rollback:** preserve registry exports, local rollback snapshot, manifests, and source trees. Avoid unnecessary exploratory registry flips.  \n> **Acceptance:** standard profile folders become the live Windows targets; source data remains intact; Luce verifies registry → shell API → disk → no orphaned active data.\n>\n> **NEXT ROUTE:** Talon → Keel execute G2/G1 → Luce verify → Don/Coda review.\n\nThat keeps this exactly where it belongs: **repair Windows truth without accidentally turning Priority 1 into the whole GCE cleanup.**"]}, "create_time": 1789413982.758296, "end_turn": true, "id": "143883d5-7369-400b-9bf9-4571b723929b", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 295, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "3a5b4f8d-fc6c-40e5-8db0-3b6a32483b77", "cited_message_idx": 129, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_c7e27f9cde2881918918109d07885442", "line_range": [19, 30], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 0, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_000000009de481fdbbcecec6f40da94a", "name": "20260914-TALON-windows-shellfolder-repair-PLAN.md", "source": "my_files", "text": null, "type": "file"}, "start_ix": 266}, {"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 686, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "3a5b4f8d-fc6c-40e5-8db0-3b6a32483b77", "cited_message_idx": 129, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_c7e27f9cde2881918918109d07885442", "line_range": [58, 61], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 0, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id":