ation closes.** It ran once and went dormant; don’t preserve a dead POC as a live surface.\n5. **`C:\\Users\\GCE_Outbox`:** **Archive candidate, not delete yet.** VoiceBridge still points to it, so repair the reference first.\n6. **Kimi grounding pointer:** **YES.** Today gave us first-hand evidence that a booting Kimi had no obvious profile-root route into GCE canon. Talon independently surfaced exactly that gap. fileciteturn2file0L49-L60\n7. **ai-inbox:** **KEEP as a tool/interface surface, not authority.** I would not mirror everything automatically to `06_HANDOFFS`; only materialized/accepted handoff events should enter the canonical bus.\n8. **`GCE_ORG\\04_PROJECTS`:** **Do not populate it with fake duplication.** Either make it an explicit pointer/index to real `Projects\\` or retire its operational meaning. My preference is a lightweight pointer/index if the Framework hierarchy needs that conceptual node.\n9. **Empty runtime shells:** **KEEP for now.** Zero cost, and today’s multi-model substitution experiment argues against prematurely decommissioning declared runtime homes.\n10. **Playa:** **Relocate out of the ops floor eventually**, because personal program material should not determine the topology of `GCE_DON`. But do that in Stage 2, not during the floor cutover.\n11. **EC8 / AG / Boxing project consolidation:** **Open later, not now.** Talon correctly held those out of this wave. fileciteturn2file0L37-L47\n\nThe architecture I want to preserve is therefore:\n\n**Stage 1 = boring physical cutover.**  \nCopy the entire working floor intact → update known dependencies/governance → test → Luce verifies → old Desktop copy becomes preserved rollback/archive.\n\n**Stage 2 = internal cleanup.**  \nOnly after the new `GCE_DON` is demonstrably live do we start deciding what inside it is legacy, personal, vestigial, or deserving of relocation.\n\nThat distinction is crucial because we finally have something that works. We should **change its parent without simultaneously changing its anatomy**.\n\nOne item I would specifically elevate before execution: Talon says `ROOT_AUTHORIZATION_REGISTRY` currently authorizes `Desktop\\GCE_DON` but is itself still marked `CANONICAL-PENDING-DON/CODA-SIGNOFF`. fileciteturn2file0L51-L60 That's actually useful timing. Rather than “sign the old registry, then immediately amend it,” I would make the G3 cutover the event that produces the **first accepted registry state with `%USERPROFILE%\\GCE_DON` as the authorized location**. Preserve the old pending document as provenance; don't rewrite its history.\n\nSo my current recommendation is:\n\n**G3 RECON: ACCEPTED**  \n**STAGE 1 END STATE: ACCEPTED IN PRINCIPLE**  \n**EXECUTION: NOT YET RELEASED**\n\nNext we should review the draft Keel execution brief specifically for whether it implements this as **copy → reference cutover → test → Luce verify → archive old location**, with no destructive move and no Stage 2 creep. If that brief passes, then you give the explicit execution gate."]}, "create_time": 1789418335.303463, "end_turn": true, "id": "78da6227-d551-472e-a461-e41648eaea07", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 388, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "47a7043d-aee2-4fb3-aa58-258934997c4f", "cited_message_idx": 281, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_214aa4e5e0688191afa618004aa535f8", "line_range": [9, 17], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 2, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000a81481fd9c676bfa500e4daf", "name": "20260914-TALON-G3-endstate-DECISION-REQUEST.md", "source": "my_files", "text": null, "type": "f