al GCE framework roots required to run those systems\n- normal Windows/system software actually in use\n\nOld Azure material, old Lares copies, old Claude/Kimi/DeepSeek environments, duplicate tool versions, stale experiment roots, obsolete configs/prompts/specs, and dead runtime homes should default to **retire/delete**, not “archive because maybe.”\n\nAnd importantly:\n\n> **Search pollution counts as operational risk.**\n>\n> If an old folder can cause grep/model discovery to surface obsolete code, prompts, configs, specs, or routing, that is a reason to remove it from the searchable live filesystem.\n\nAfter Talon finishes Lares, give Luce this:\n\n> # LUCE — WHOLE-MACHINE FINAL CLEANUP RECON\n>\n> **SEAT:** Luce  \n> **OCCUPANT:** Big Pickle  \n> **MODE:** whole-machine truth recon  \n> **EXECUTION AUTHORITY:** NONE\n>\n> ## DON RULING\n>\n> We are ending archaeology.\n>\n> The objective is to reduce this machine to:\n>\n> **CURRENT TRUTH + CURRENT PROJECTS + REQUIRED SYSTEM SOFTWARE + COMPACT RECOVERY EVIDENCE**\n>\n> not a museum of prior environments.\n>\n> Old material that can pollute grep/search/model discovery is operational clutter even if technically harmless.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## ACTIVE ALLOWLIST\n>\n> Treat these as presumptively live/valuable:\n>\n> - VoiceBridge\n> - current Web scraper work\n> - Command Center\n> - DevPad\n> - Roundtable / crowdsourcing\n> - Amazon Bedrock work\n> - canonical GCE framework required to support current operation\n> - `Projects\\` current organized projects\n> - Edge Crew\n> - Casa Companion\n> - current Windows/software dependencies actually required by the above\n>\n> Everything else must prove current value.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## RECON SCOPE\n>\n> Inspect the machine in four surfaces:\n>\n> ### A. Desktop\n> `C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\Desktop`\n>\n> ### B. User profile\n> `C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother`\n>\n> including obvious tool/config roots, Documents, Downloads, local GCE roots, hidden dotfolders where relevant.\n>\n> ### C. Users root\n> `C:\\Users`\n>\n> Identify real Windows profiles versus ordinary folders/pseudo-user roots.\n>\n> ### D. System root\n> `C:\\`\n>\n> Identify non-system top-level folders and legacy project/runtime roots.\n>\n> Do not waste effort recursively cataloging Windows, Program Files, ProgramData, or known OS internals unless a suspicious custom dependency points there.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## CLASSIFICATION RULE\n>\n> Every suspicious/custom root gets exactly one classification:\n>\n> `KEEP-LIVE`\n>\n> `KEEP-SYSTEM`\n>\n> `MOVE-TO-CANONICAL`\n>\n> `MANIFEST-ONLY-THEN-DELETE`\n>\n> `DELETE-CANDIDATE`\n>\n> `ADMIN-DELETE-CANDIDATE`\n>\n> `HOLD — REAL LIVE DEPENDENCY`\n>\n> Avoid `UNKNOWN` unless evidence genuinely cannot resolve it.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## PRESERVATION RULE\n>\n> Do not assume old = archive.\n>\n> For retired material, preserve full payload only when:\n>\n> - there is meaningful restore value;\n> - the content is unique and human-authored;\n> - no current successor exists;\n> - Don could reasonably want to restore it.\n>\n> Otherwise preserve only a compact ledger entry:\n>\n> `ITEM | FORMER PURPOSE | LAST USED | RETIRED DATE | SUCCESSOR | RESTORE VALUE | ACTION`\n>\n> Then recommend deletion of payload.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## SEARCH-POLLUTION RULE\n>\n> Flag old trees containing obsolete:\n>\n> - prompts\n> - specs\n> - AGENTS/bootstrap files\n> - configs\n> - scripts\n> - source code\n> - model instructions\n> - handoffs\n>\n> that could be rediscovered by broad grep/search.\n>\n> These should be prioritized for removal from the live/searchable filesystem.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## CREDENTIAL RULE\n>\n> Old credentials inside retired trees do **not** automatically block cleanup.\n>\n> If the surrounding system is retired and Don has not named the credential as currently required:\n>\n> classify it:\n>\n> `RETIRED — DO NOT REUSE`\n>\n> and recommend deletion with the legacy payload.\n>\n> Do not create rotation projects merely to delete dead environments.\n>\n> Exception: clearly current credentials supporting the allowlisted active systems.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## SPECIAL AREAS TO RESOLVE\n>\n> Include the already-known unresolved items:\n>\n> - DeepSeek Terminal\n> - `_Deprecated-Claude`\n> - `Desktop Archive 2026-07-09`\n> - Documents / betting-map split\n> - `C:\\Users\\claude`\n> - `GCE_Outbox`\n> - archived-GCE empty admin shells\n> - `GCE_Applied_AI_Team` empty retired peer root\n> - CodexSandboxOffline\n> - `inetpub`\n> - remaining Lares residue if any\n> - stale Azure material\n> - stale Claude/Kimi/DeepSeek roots/configs\n> - duplicate old versions of VoiceBridge/web scraper/Command Center/Roundtable\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## DELIVERABLE\n>\n> Do **not** return hundreds of files.\n>\n> Return a decision-oriented machine map:\n>\n> `KEEP-LIVE ROOTS`\n>\n> `KEEP-SYSTEM ROOTS`\n>\n> `DELETE NOW`\n>\n> `DELETE WITH ADMIN`\n>\n> `MOVE TO CANONICAL`\n>\n> `MANIFEST-ONLY THEN DELETE`\n>\n> `REAL HOLDS`\n>\n> `SEARCH-POLLUTION HOTSPOTS`\n>\n> `TOTAL ESTIMATED SPACE RECOVERABLE`\n>\n> `TOP 20 ACTIONS MAX`\n>\n> `TALON EXECUTION WAVE`\n>\n> `DON DECISIONS NEEDED`\n>\n> The recommended Talon wave should aim to perform the majority of remaining cleanup in **one execution pass**, not another chain of tiny waves.\n>\n> Write one durable finding + one Don handoff.\n>\n> **HARD STOP:** recon only.\n>\n> **NEXT ROUTE:** Luce → Don/Coda one decision review → Talon consolidated cleanup → Luce final whole-machine verification.\n\nThat is where I want us now: **one comprehensive map, one cleanup execution, one verification.**\n\nWe should be able to finish this without turning tomorrow into Day 3 of filesystem archaeology."]}, "create_time": 1789529299.404712, "end_turn": true, "id": "5ba1f66d-2957-4162-839c-18a97dd1b742", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_t