ique human-authored delta?\n> - current process references?\n> - current config/bootstrap references?\n> - current Git repo/branch?\n>\n> Do not recursively diff dependency trees like:\n>\n> - node_modules\n> - venv\n> - build\n> - dist\n> - caches\n> - downloaded models\n>\n> unless needed to prove a dependency.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## GIT / REPO AUTHORITY\n>\n> For each real repo:\n>\n> determine:\n>\n> - `.git` presence\n> - remote\n> - branch\n> - dirty state\n> - whether multiple physical clones exist\n> - whether one copy is ahead/diverged\n>\n> Do not push, pull, commit, reset, checkout, or modify.\n>\n> Flag:\n>\n> `DIVERGED COPY`\n>\n> `DIRTY UNIQUE COPY`\n>\n> `CLEAN DUPLICATE`\n>\n> `NON-REPO MIRROR`\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## SEARCH-POLLUTION RECON\n>\n> Flag project trees containing stale:\n>\n> - AGENTS\n> - CLAUDE\n> - bootstrap docs\n> - prompts\n> - architecture specs\n> - configs\n> - source\n> - handoffs\n> - `.env.example`\n> - old entrypoints\n>\n> that could be surfaced by broad search and mistaken for current authority.\n>\n> Return:\n>\n> `SAFE PROJECT SEARCH ROOTS`\n>\n> `AMBIGUOUS PROJECT ROOTS`\n>\n> `COLD/ARCHIVE ROOTS`\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## REQUIRED OUTPUT\n>\n> Do not return a file dump.\n>\n> Return:\n>\n> ### 1. PROJECT ESTATE MAP\n>\n> Major current projects and physical roots.\n>\n> ### 2. CASA COMPANION AUTHORITY MAP\n>\n> All Casa generations/copies and one recommended canonical authority.\n>\n> ### 3. EDGE CREW AUTHORITY MAP\n>\n> Canonical, worktrees, stale copies, archive copies.\n>\n> ### 4. OTHER DUPLICATE PROJECTS\n>\n> Any other multi-copy projects.\n>\n> ### 5. GIT / DIVERGENCE RISKS\n>\n> Unique dirty/diverged copies that must not be blindly deleted.\n>\n> ### 6. SEARCH-POLLUTION RISKS\n>\n> ### 7. STALE-CANDIDATES\n>\n> Use the ~60-day + no-consumer rule.\n>\n> ### 8. TRUE HOLDS\n>\n> Exact reason each must remain.\n>\n> ### 9. DON DECISION TABLE\n>\n> Maximum 15 items:\n>\n> `PROJECT/ROOT | FACTUAL STATE | CURRENT CONSUMER | UNIQUE DELTA? | CANONICAL? | LUCE RECOMMENDATION`\n>\n> ### 10. TALON CLEANUP CANDIDATES\n>\n> One consolidated project-cleanup wave if evidence supports it.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## HARD GUARDRAILS\n>\n> Do not:\n>\n> - delete\n> - move\n> - merge\n> - restore\n> - commit\n> - pull/push\n> - rewrite Git state\n> - change project configs\n> - choose a canonical project solely from timestamps\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## FINAL QUESTIONS\n>\n> End with:\n>\n> **1. Does every active project now have one physically clear canonical root?**\n>\n> **2. Where do duplicate project authorities still exist?**\n>\n> **3. Which project copies can Talon safely retire in one pass?**\n>\n> Write one durable finding + one Don handoff.\n>\n> **NEXT ROUTE:** Luce → Don/Coda review → one Talon project-reduction wave.\n\nThis is the right recon to run while Talon finishes the machine pass. The Casa section should give us the actual truth instead of continuing to reason from folder names."]}, "create_time": 1789534234.098169, "end_turn": true, "id": "1f8fb341-bad7-4dd3-a7de-ef0fd169d655", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "c80908f5-4915-4e4e-b2fb-99d48309a0f1", "request_id": "277e433e-c3c6-4bcc-bb52-6fb7effd89fd", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "d6156093-7f6f-475f-a9c7-a2a72de4a642", "turn_id": "07746c52-5f4c-4573-ab26-546c9918444e", "working_turn_id": "d6156093-7f6f-475f-a9c7-a2a72de4a642"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1789534267.91315, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "co