 them type correctly without manual repair.\n>\n> Examples:\n>\n> `load luce bootstrap`\n>\n> `load talon bootstrap`\n>\n> `review the router`\n>\n> `open voicebridge`\n>\n> `verify the handoff`\n>\n> `stop`\n>\n> ## ANALYZE LOGS FOR COMMAND-SHAPED UTTERANCES\n>\n> Identify utterances that are:\n>\n> - short\n> - imperative\n> - framework/tool-heavy\n> - likely intended as terminal/OpenCode commands\n>\n> For each, compare transcription quality against likely intended command vocabulary.\n>\n> ## PRIORITIZE ERRORS THAT BREAK COMMANDS\n>\n> Especially flag errors in:\n>\n> - seat names\n> - bootstrap/load grammar\n> - tool names\n> - command verbs\n> - folder/framework terms\n> - short phrases where one wrong token changes meaning\n>\n> ## RETURN CANDIDATES AS\n>\n> `RAW TRANSCRIPTION`\n>\n> `LIKELY COMMAND`\n>\n> `ERROR TOKEN`\n>\n> `CANONICAL TOKEN`\n>\n> `COUNT`\n>\n> `CONFIDENCE`\n>\n> `SAFE AUTO-CORRECT?`\n>\n> `WOULD THIS BREAK EXECUTION? YES/NO`\n>\n> ## CLASSIFY\n>\n> `COMMAND-CRITICAL AUTO-FIX`\n>\n> `USEFUL GENERAL NORMALIZATION`\n>\n> `WATCHLIST`\n>\n> `DO NOT TOUCH`\n>\n> ## SPECIAL TEST SET\n>\n> Build a compact spoken test set of 15–20 commands covering:\n>\n> Luce\n>\n> Talon\n>\n> Coda\n>\n> Chiave\n>\n> Calibro\n>\n> Corrado\n>\n> Falcon\n>\n> Kimi\n>\n> Kalshi\n>\n> VoiceBridge\n>\n> OpenCode\n>\n> bootstrap\n>\n> verify\n>\n> reconcile\n>\n> stop\n>\n> Do not modify code yet.\n>\n> ## RETURN\n>\n> `COMMAND RELIABILITY FINDINGS`\n>\n> `COMMAND-CRITICAL FIXES`\n>\n> `TEST COMMAND SET`\n>\n> `READY FOR IMPLEMENTATION: YES/NO`\n>\n> Then STOP.\n\nThat’s the right lens now: **make your spoken operating commands dependable first; general proofreading is secondary.**"]}, "create_time": 1789611157.149639, "end_turn": true, "id": "51f7c1ee-aadf-485f-a7a9-656cc602f82f", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "f