 now, I think this will fall on Big Pickle with what you're saying, right? We should have had enough text to understand what I'm malforming and what needs to be corrected. Even if we go one by one. It's not a lot, but also I want to get the commands on how I operate. Devpad screen 1, go to Luce. What can we do? "]}, "create_time": 1789611194.539, "end_turn": null, "id": "e0e25245-437d-4a9f-8e61-2da897cd3c13", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "message_source": null, "request_id": "adc1ada8-9103-4ebc-be3c-7f23e1772a79", "selected_sources": [], "serialization_metadata": {"custom_symbol_offsets": []}, "turn_exchange_id": "1dd8ee2d-65a3-4239-95cf-5bc86e5620db", "turn_id": "305d25da-8783-4a19-9221-47dd90dc5460", "working_turn_id": "1dd8ee2d-65a3-4239-95cf-5bc86e5620db"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1789611219.757274, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yes — this is where Big Pickle should earn its keep.\n\nYou’ve got enough real VoiceBridge history now that we should stop thinking only in terms of “fix these five words” and instead answer the bigger operating question:\n\n**What spoken commands can Don reliably use to control his working environment?**\n\nThe target you just described is something like:\n\n> “DevPad screen one, go to Luce.”\n>\n> “Screen two, open Talon.”\n>\n> “Switch to OpenCode.”\n>\n> “Load Luce bootstrap.”\n>\n> “Go back to DevPad.”\n>\n> “Next terminal.”\n>\n> “Focus screen three.”\n\nThat’s no longer just transcription correction. It’s **voice command grammar + window targeting + navigation**.\n\nAnd yes, Big Pickle should first inspect what VoiceBridge already supports before we invent anything. We want to know:\n\n- what commands already exist\n- whether it can identify/focus windows\n- whether it can send hotkeys\n- whether it can target monitor/screen/window numbers\n- whether it can launch shortcuts/apps\n- whether Cockpit already has hooks for this\n- what can be added cheaply without turning VoiceBridge into another giant framework\n\nI’d give Big Pickle this next:\n\n> # BIG PICKLE — VOICEBRIDGE COMMAND SURFACE + DESKTOP CONTROL RECON\n>\n> **MODE:** bounded recon only  \n> **OBJECTIVE:** determine what Don can currently control by voice across terminals, OpenCode sessions, DevPad, and desktop windows, and identify the smallest command grammar needed for practical hands-free operation.\n>\n> ## PRIMARY USE CASE\n>\n> Don wants to move between working windows and issue commands by voice.\n>\n> Example desired phrases:\n>\n> - `DevPad screen one`\n> - `go to Luce`\n> - `go to Talon`\n> - `screen two`\n> - `next terminal`\n> - `previous terminal`\n> - `focus OpenCode`\n> - `load Luce bootstrap`\n> - `load Talon bootstrap`\n> - `open VoiceBridge`\n> - `go back to DevPad`\n>\n> Do not assume these exist.\n>\n> ## 1. INVENTORY CURRENT COMMAND CAPABILITY\n>\n> Inspect the canonical VoiceBridge implementation and identify all existing command/control mechanisms:\n>\n> - spoken command parser\n> - wake-word command handling\n> - continuous mode behavior\n> - keyboard/hotkey injection\n> - window focus/switching\n> - process launching\n> - app targeting\n> - monitor/screen awareness\n> - terminal targeting\n> - Cockpit controls\n> - clipboard/paste/send-enter behaviors\n>\n> Return exact source files/functions responsible.\n>\n> ## 2. EXISTING SPOKEN COMMANDS\n>\n> Extract every currently recognized command phrase or command family.\n>\n> Return:\n>\n> `COMMAND`\n>\n> `ACTION`\n>\n> `IMPLEMENTATION PATH`\n>\n> `WORKS IN CONTINUOUS MODE?`\n>\n> `REQUIRES WAKE WORD?`\n>\n> `EXECUTION RISK`\n>\n> Do not infer commands that are not actually implemented.\n>\n> ## 3. WINDOW / TERMINAL CONTROL\n>\n> Determine whether VoiceBridge can currently:\n>\n> - identify active window\n> - focus a named window\n> - cycle windows\n> - cycle terminal windows\n> - select by monitor\n> - select by window title\n> - select OpenCode sessions by seat/title\n> - send keystrokes to a non-focused window\n> - launch/focus DevPad\n>\n> For each return:\n>\n> `SUPPORTED NOW`\n>\n> `PARTIALLY SUPPORTED`\n>\n> `NOT SUPPORTED`\n>\n> `SMALLEST IMPLEMENTATION PATH`\n>\n> ## 4. DEVPad / OPENCODE TARGETING\n>\n> Inspect current running-window conventions and determine whether these can be addressed deterministically:\n>\n> - DevPad\n> - OpenCode\n> - Luce session\n> - Talon session\n> - Coda session\n> - other terminal windows\n>\n> Look for:\n>\n> - window titles\n> - process names\n> - session names\n> - terminal titles\n> - monitor placement\n>\n> Determine the most reliable targeting mechanism:\n>\n> `WINDOW TITLE`\n>\n> `PROCESS`\n>\n> `SCREEN POSITION`\n>\n> `MONITOR NUMBER`\n>\n> `SESSION NAME`\n>\n> or combination.\n>\n> ## 5. COMMAND GRAMMAR DESIGN\n>\n> Based on current capabilities, propose a **small, natural command grammar** for Don.\n>\n> Keep it conversational and short.\n>\n> Example categories:\n>\n> ### Navigation\n>\n> `go to Luce`\n>\n> `go to Talon`\n>\n> `next terminal`\n>\n> `previous terminal`\n>\n> `DevPad`\n>\n> ### Screen targeting\n>\n> `screen one`\n>\n> `screen two`\n>\n> `move this to screen two`\n>\n> ### Seat operations\n>\n> `load Luce bootstrap`\n>\n> `load Talon bootstrap`\n>\n> ### Utility\n>\n> `open VoiceBridge`\n>\n> `stop listening`\n>\n> `start listening`\n>\n> `reconnect`\n>\n> Do not design more than necessary.\n>\n> ## 6. LOG-BASED VOCABULARY SUPPORT\n>\n> Use recent VoiceBridge logs to identify malformed versions of words needed for the proposed command grammar.\n>\n> Prioritize:\n>\n> - DevPad\n> - Luce\n> - Talon\n> - Coda\n> - Chiave\n> - Calibro\n> - Corrado\n> - Falcon\n> - OpenCode\n> - VoiceBridge\n> - bootstrap\n> - screen\n> - terminal\n> - next\n> - previous\n> - focus\n> - go to\n>\n> Return only real observed errors or credible near-matches.\n>\n> ## 7. PRACTICAL COMMAND SET\n>\n> Produce a first **10–20 command operating vocabulary** Don could realistically use every day.\n>\n> Divide into:\n>\n> `WORKS TODAY`\n>\n> `SMALL CHANGE REQUIRED`\n>\n> `FUTURE / DO NOT BUILD YET`\n>\n> ## 8. RETURN\n>\n> `CURRENT COMMAND SURFACE`\n>\n> `WINDOW CONTROL CAPABILITY`\n>\n> `DEVPad/OPENCODE TARGETING OPTIONS`\n>\n> `CURRENT COMMANDS THAT ALREADY WORK`\n>\n> `COMMANDS REQUIRING SMALL CHANGES`\n>\n> `RECOMMENDED DAILY COMMAND VOCABULARY`\n>\n> `LOG-BASED PRONUNCIATION/CORRECTION NEEDS`\n>\n> `SMALLEST NEXT IMPLEMENTATION`\n>\n> Then STOP.\n>\n> ## HARD GUARDRAILS\n>\n> - no code changes\n> - no UI redesign\n> - no giant command framework\n> - no new agent architecture\n> - no speculative automation\n> - no destructive actions\n\nThat will tell us whether **“DevPad screen 1, go to Luce”** is already close to possible or whether the clean first step is something simpler like:\n\n**“go to Luce” → focus the terminal/window whose title contains `Luce`**\n\nand\n\n**“DevPad” → focus the DevPad window**\n\nThen we build outward one command at a time."]}, "create_time": 1789611196.265085, "end_turn": true, "id": "d3332246-384c-4f26-901c-3e45b5b36cd6", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "b467c5f7-8fe6-4293-afd3-164a48785d8b", "request_id": "adc1ada8-9103-4ebc-be3c-7f23e1772a79", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "1dd8ee2d-65a3-4239-95cf-5bc86e5620db", "turn_id": "0d571626-3c9f-481c-a403-f8a9de3edc3e", "working_turn_id": "1dd8ee2d-65a3-4239-95cf-5bc86e5620db"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1789611225.785343, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content": "Worked for a couple of seconds", "content_type": "reasoning_recap"}, "create_time": 1789611198.633038, "end_turn": false, "id": "b467c5f7-8fe6-4293-afd3-164a48785d8b", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finished_duration_sec": 1, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "cd2f9be4-6013-43ab-bfd6-cbdf89d77b1f", "reasoning_end_time": 1789611198.3139277, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1789611196.352603, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "adc1ada8-9103-4ebc-be3c-7f23e1772a79", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "1dd8ee2d-65a3-4239-95cf-5bc86e5620db", "turn_id": "0d571626-3c9f-481c-a403-f8a9de3edc3e", "working_turn_id": "1dd8ee2d-65a3-4239-95cf-5bc86e5620db"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["CURRENT COMMAND SURFACE\nEntry flow — continuous mode is the live default (config.json continuous: true):\n- Every ASR final → _handle_final (src/voice_bridge.py:364) → continuous branch (:372): session commands (quit/pause/resume/help), else lock_target_window() + _dispatch (:393-394). Wake-word gate exists (_find_wake_word :354, _is_armed :351, 12s timeout) but is off.\n- _dispatch (:417): corrections map → me→Don regex → handle_command (voice_commands.py:263, leading-word longest-match) → execute_command (voice_commands.py:498) or profile phrase (voice_profile.py:54/:61) or verbatim typing (:479).\nMechanisms / homes:\nMechanism\tWhere\nSpoken command parser (leading-word, longest-match)\tsrc/voice_commands.py:263-277\nCommand phrase table\tsrc/voice_commands.py:28-211\nAction executor (hotkeys/macros/launchers)\tsrc/voice_commands.py:498-574\nWindow/terminal enumerate+focus (Windows API)\tsrc/voice_commands.py:407-492\nProfile slash/hotkey phrases\tvoice-profile.json → src/voice_profile.py\nKeyboard injection (into locked/focused window)\tsrc/keyboard_input.py:23-51\nMic capture + supervisor\tsrc/capture.py, voice_bridge.py:492-541\nCockpit (queue + route buttons)\tsrc/queue_panel.py (UI-side only; no voice target)\nSession macros (proofread/concise/format)\tsrc/llm.py via voice_commands._macro\nScreenshot\tsrc/screenshot.py\nEXISTING SPOKEN COMMANDS (all live, no invention)\nCOMMAND (representative)\tACTION\tPATH\nstop/start listening, wake up\tpause/resume\t_handle_final :378-385\nquit / exit\tshutdown\t:374\ndelete that / word / line / sentence, clear all\tclipboard/select hotkeys\t_COMMANDS→execute_command\ncopy/cut/paste/undo/redo/save/select all\thotkeys into focused window\tsame\nsend/enter/return, new line, tab, space, punctuation\ttype/press\tsame\ncaps on/off\tcapslock\tsame\narrows, page up/down\tpress\tsame\nnext terminal / previous terminal\tcycle terminal windows\t_cycle_terminal :468\nwindow a / b / c / d (+ Kimi#8 aliases)\tfocus terminal index 0-3\t_activate_terminal_by_index :459\nscreen one/two/three, jump left/center/right\tsnap focused window via Win+Shift+Arrow\t_move_window :476\nclose/new tab, new window, close window\thotkeys\tsame\nminimize/maximize/show desktop/task view\tWin hotkeys\tsame\nalt tab / go back / forward / refresh / find / cancel\thotkeys\tsame\nscreenshot / take a screenshot\tfull-desktop to clipboard\tvoice_commands.py:302\nproofread / concise / format\tselect→LLM rewrite→paste\t_macro :369\ncockpit / handoff\tos.startfile launcher .cmds\tvoice_commands.py:313-331\nopencode / claude / kimi profile phrases (branch, new session, sessions, share, compact, help…)\ttyped slash cmd or ctrl+x f into focused terminal\tvoice-profile.json\nSession-only (never in continuous error path): none — continuous covers everything; wake-word mode is dormant.\nWINDOW / TERMINAL CONTROL\nCapability\tStatus\tSmallest path\nIdentify active window\tPARTIAL (GetForegroundWindow in keyboard_input.py:26; titles enumerated voice_commands.py:422)\tno change needed\nFocus a named window\tNOT SUPPORTED\t_focus_named_window(title_sub): reuse _list_visible_windows+_activate_window\nCycle windows (alt-tab style)\tNOT SUPPORTED (only terminals)\talias _cycle_terminal for all windows\nCycle terminal windows\tSUPPORTED (windows only, not tabs)\toptionally send ctrl+tab for WT tabs\nSelect by monitor\tPARTIAL (snap-focused-window only)\tmonitor-rect match in _activate_window\nSelect by window title\tNOT SUPPORTED\tsee named focus above\nSelect OpenCode seat by title\tNOT SUPPORTED\tdedicated titled WT windows per seat\nKeystrokes to non-focused window\tNOT SUPPORTED (writes go to foreground / ARM-time target only, keyboard_input.py:42)\tPostMessage/SendInput w/ hwnd — larger work, don't build\nLaunch/focus DevPad\tNOT SUPPORTED (cockpit/handoff exist; DevPad has no launcher)\tone profile entry → explorer.exe path or titled window\nDEVPAD / OPENCODE TARGETING OPTIONS\nObserved reality (live process scan): one WindowsTerminal window (\"Windows PowerShell\"), plus VoiceBridge/Brave/Outlook/Word. OpenCode seats and DevPad have no dedicated titled windows today.\n- Targeting by window title on dedicated per-seat Windows Terminal windows (wt.exe -w new --title Luce …) = most reliable and deterministic — titles are the only stable, human-meaningful handle.\n- Process name works to bucket (python/opencode) but can't disambiguate tabs.\n- Monitor number is feasible and stable as a secondary key (Win32 MonitorFromWindow).\n- Session name is not exposed in titles by default — not usable without a wrapper (don't build).\nCOMMANDS REQUIRING SMALL CHANGES\n1. reconnect — the UI button exists (_reconnect_now, voice_bridge.py:672) but no voice alias; \"reconnect\" currently types as text.\n2. go to \\<seat\\> (Luce/Talon/Coda/…) — needs one _focus_named_window + a handful of phrases (needs seats running in titled windows).\n3. load \\<seat\\> bootstrap — zero new infra: it's just dictation into a focused opencode session, or one voice-profile.json phrase that types it.\n4. open VoiceBridge — self-focus by title.\n5. DevPad — launcher alias (open folder/session window), not a framework.\nRECOMMENDED DAILY COMMAND VOCABULARY\nWORKS TODAY (voice, no change): stop listening · start listening · new line · send/enter · copy that · paste it · undo · delete that / word / line · select all · proofread / concise / format · next terminal / previous terminal · window a/b/c/d · screen one / two / three · screenshot · cockpit · handoff · opencode profile phrases (new session, sessions, branch) · quit.\nSMALL CHANGE REQUIRED: reconnect · go to Luce / Talon / Coda / DevPad · open VoiceBridge · focus OpenCode · load Luce bootstrap / load Talon bootstrap (profile phrase).\nFUTURE / DO NOT BUILD: per-monitor seat grid · voice-driven queue-panel routing · keystrokes into background windows · OpenCode session multiplexer/watchdog.\nLOG-BASED PRONUNCIATION/CORRECTION NEEDS\nClean words across the corpus — nothing blocking the grammar:\n- DevPad → \"dev pad\"/\"devpad\" (7×, no misfires) · opencode → \"open code\" (11×) · bootstrap (40×) · screen (5×) · terminal(s) (14×) · focus(ed) (16×) · next/go to (67×).\n- \"go to \\<Name\\>\" = zero occurrences in corpus → grammar is net-new; all constituent words already transcribe cleanly.\n- Latent gap only: Luci→Luce (2 historical), Calibra→Calibro (1) — unrelated to grammar.\n- Collision check: \"go to sleep\" cannot trigger sleep (leading-word parser, \"sleep\" is not a prefix), so no pause misfire.\nSMALLEST NEXT IMPLEMENTATION\n1. _focus_named_window(title_substr) in voice_commands.py (reuses existing _list_visible_windows/_activate_window).\n2. Launch seats as titled WT windows (wt.exe -w new --title <seat>) and a phrase table (like voice-profile.json): go to Luce / Talon / Coda / DevPad / OpenCode / VoiceBridge.\n3. Voice alias reconnect → existing _reconnect_now.\n4. load \\<seat\\> bootstrap as profile phrases typed into the focused seat.\nThat's ~6 mapping rows + 1 small helper — no architecture, no new agent machinery. Not built in this pass."]}, "create_time": 1789611549.913, "end_turn": null, "id": "815753ab-0f21-4b6c-aff8-422a9ea51572", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "message_source": null, "request_id": "98138192-272e-4b3f-9da7-a39c7822a64d", "selected_sources": [], "serialization_metadata": {"custom_symbol_offsets": []}, "turn_exchange_id": "b47317a2-a228-4cdb-8ced-3ea7d69c18e3", "turn_id": "acd31d93-a5b6-4d8d-a0d0-011256edeb8d", "working_turn_id": "b47317a2-a228-4cdb-8ced-3ea7d69c18e3"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1789611572.045414, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["This is actually a very good result. We already have much more command surface than it looked like.\n\nThe key finding is: **you do not need a new voice-control framework.** VoiceBridge already has the parser, hotkeys, window enumeration, terminal cycling, screen movement, profile phrases, macros, and launcher actions. What’s missing is mostly **named-window targeting**.\n\nThat means your real day-to-day command model can become:\n\n- `go to Luce`\n- `go to Talon`\n- `go to Coda`\n- `go to DevPad`\n- `go to OpenCode`\n- `next terminal`\n- `previous terminal`\n- `screen one`\n- `screen two`\n- `screen three`\n- `load Luce bootstrap`\n- `load Talon bootstrap`\n- `reconnect`\n- `cockpit`\n- `handoff`\n- `proofread`\n- `send`\n\nThe cleanest implementation is exactly what Big Pickle found: **give each seat/window a deterministic title, then VoiceBridge focuses by title substring.** That is much better than trying to guess by process or physical screen position.\n\nSo I would do the small implementation now. Give Big Pickle this:\n\n> # BIG PICKLE — VOICEBRIDGE NAMED WINDOW CONTROL IMPLEMENTATION\n>\n> **MODE:** bounded implementation  \n> **OBJECTIVE:** add the smallest practical voice-navigation layer so Don can move between DevPad/OpenCode/seat windows by name.\n>\n> ## ACCEPTED RECON\n>\n> Existing VoiceBridge already supports:\n>\n> - command parser\n> - terminal cycling\n> - screen movement\n> - hotkeys\n> - launcher commands\n> - profile phrases\n> - session macros\n>\n> Missing capability is deterministic named-window focus.\n>\n> Do not redesign VoiceBridge.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## 1. ADD NAMED WINDOW FOCUS\n>\n> In `src\\voice_commands.py`, add the smallest helper needed to:\n>\n> `focus visible window whose title contains <requested substring>`\n>\n> Reuse the existing:\n>\n> - visible-window enumeration\n> - `_activate_window`\n>\n> Matching should be case-insensitive.\n>\n> If zero matches:\n>\n> - fail safely\n> - do not type the command into the current terminal\n>\n> If multiple matches:\n>\n> - use deterministic behavior or report ambiguity\n> - do not randomly choose\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## 2. ADD ONLY THESE INITIAL VOICE ROUTES\n>\n> Add:\n>\n> `go to Luce`\n>\n> `go to Talon`\n>\n> `go to Coda`\n>\n> `go to DevPad`\n>\n> `go to OpenCode`\n>\n> `go to VoiceBridge`\n>\n> These should call named-window focus.\n>\n> Do not add every possible seat yet.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## 3. TITLED WINDOW CONVENTION\n>\n> Determine the smallest reliable way to launch/open seat terminals with stable titles such as:\n>\n> `Luce`\n>\n> `Talon`\n>\n> `Coda`\n>\n> `OpenCode`\n>\n> Prefer Windows Terminal's native title support.\n>\n> Do not build a session manager.\n>\n> Return the exact launch convention used.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## 4. BOOTSTRAP PHRASES\n>\n> Add simple profile phrases:\n>\n> `load Luce bootstrap`\n>\n> `load Talon bootstrap`\n>\n> `load Coda bootstrap`\n>\n> These should type the literal command into the currently focused terminal/OpenCode session.\n>\n> They should not themselves perform seat routing outside OpenCode.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## 5. RECONNECT\n>\n> Add:\n>\n> `reconnect`\n>\n> routed to the existing VoiceBridge reconnect function.\n>\n> Do not create a second reconnect implementation.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## 6. TEST\n>\n> Verify:\n>\n> `go to Luce`\n>\n> focuses a window titled Luce.\n>\n> `go to Talon`\n>\n> focuses Talon.\n>\n> `go to Coda`\n>\n> focuses Coda.\n>\n> `go to DevPad`\n>\n> focuses DevPad if present.\n>\n> `go to VoiceBridge`\n>\n> focuses VoiceBridge.\n>\n> `next terminal`\n>\n> still works.\n>\n> `screen one/two/three`\n>\n> still works.\n>\n> `load Luce bootstrap`\n>\n> types exactly that command into the active target.\n>\n> `reconnect`\n>\n> invokes the existing reconnect path.\n>\n> Unknown or absent window names must not produce destructive behavior.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## HARD GUARDRAILS\n>\n> - no new command framework\n> - no background-window keystroke injection\n> - no session multiplexer\n> - no monitor-grid system\n> - no Cockpit redesign\n> - no agent changes\n> - no fuzzy window matching beyond safe title-substring matching\n>\n> ## RETURN\n>\n> `NAMED WINDOW FOCUS: PASS/FAIL`\n>\n> `WINDOW TITLE CONVENTION`\n>\n> `GO TO LUCE: PASS/FAIL`\n>\n> `GO TO TALON: PASS/FAIL`\n>\n> `GO TO CODA: PASS/FAIL`\n>\n> `GO TO DEVPAD: PASS/FAIL`\n>\n> `GO TO VOICEBRIDGE: PASS/FAIL`\n>\n> `BOOTSTRAP PHRASES: PASS/FAIL`\n>\n> `RECONNECT: PASS/FAIL`\n>\n> `EXISTING COMMAND REGRESSION TEST`\n>\n> `FILES MODIFIED`\n>\n> `DEVIATIONS`\n>\n> Then STOP.\n\nOnce that works, your operating pattern gets much closer to what you were describing:\n\n**“Go to Luce.” → “load Luce bootstrap.” → dictate work → “go to Talon.” → dictate next instruction → “go to DevPad.”**\n\nThat is the first genuinely useful hands-free control layer."]}, "create_time": 1789611552.252321, "end_turn": true, "id": "e6d15445-b139-4f4a-a197-97a6995c53e