he explicitly named current data feed/output root for that work item.\n\nIt should **not** search:\n\n`C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother`\n\n`Desktop\\mlb-data-system\\EC8`\n\nold WNBA trees\n\nhistorical configs\n\narchive/provenance material\n\nunless the brief specifically authorizes historical discovery.\n\nThere is another clue in the transcript: Falcon itself noticed it was launched from the profile root and said that was the “wrong launch home” for strict resolution, even though the router correctly loaded its identity. fileciteturn5file0L15-L18 That does **not** mean the root router is broken. It means the **execution search root and identity routing are two different things**.\n\nSo I think the fix is very small. Falcon needs a standing search rule roughly like:\n\n> For bounded EdgeCrew Quant work, operate only inside the work-item anchor and explicitly named current data roots. Do not perform profile-wide discovery, search historical sports systems, or inspect stale configs unless the work item explicitly requests historical recovery. If the required dataset cannot be found inside the authorized roots, return `BLOCKED — DATA ANCHOR REQUIRED` instead of widening scope.\n\nThat is the missing guardrail.\n\nAnd I agree with your instinct: if you tell Falcon **“do EdgeCrew data”**, it should not be wandering through WNBA or old config just because those words happen to match `calibration`, `picks`, or `frozen`.\n\nI would **not redesign Falcon**. I’d have Big Pickle do one narrow recon on Falcon’s current `AGENTS.md` / load-root to answer one question:\n\n**“Where should the current-work search boundary be enforced so Falcon searches the active EdgeCrew Quant world first and stops instead of widening into historical systems?”**\n\nThen we make the smallest correction there."]}, "create_time": 1789678910.059547, "end_turn": true, "id": "d46fe882-5698-4966-b481-2f9f02204da4", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search