oblem has been identified.\n\nThe Windows registry / shell-folder state appears to have created a second effective Desktop path that points into locations such as Documents / Downloads.\n\nResult:\n\n- Windows paths are not behaving as assumed.\n- Desktop / Documents / user-folder boundaries are blurred.\n- Framework artifacts may be resolving into unexpected locations.\n- Models and tools may be searching or writing against different physical locations while believing they are operating in the same environment.\n\nThis must be treated as an **environment truth problem first**, not as a folder-cleanup problem.\n\n### Immediate rule\n\nDo not reorganize, rename, delete, consolidate, or move Framework material until the actual Windows shell / registry routing is verified.\n\nThis investigation begins in the next new chat.\n\n---\n\n## 2. DUPLICATE FRAMEWORK / USER STRUCTURES\n\nA second major issue is confirmed conceptually:\n\nThere is unnecessary duplication between Framework structures under the user-account environment and duplicate structures maintained on the Desktop.\n\nThis produces:\n\n- duplicate inboxes,\n- duplicate folder trees,\n- ambiguous handoffs,\n- ambiguous model search locations,\n- unclear source-of-truth paths,\n- and weak grounding of models in their actual identity homes.\n\n### Working direction\n\nThe likely operating model is to use the **Users / user-account structure as the primary operating location**, rather than maintaining parallel Framework structures under both the user environment and Desktop.\n\nThis is not yet permission to delete or merge anything.\n\nThe first task is to establish:\n\n**what exists → what Windows actually points to → what each model currently loads → what should remain active.**\n\nOnly then should consolidation occur.\n\n---\n\n## 3. CHAT SCRAPING / CHAT BACKUP / REORGANIZATION\n\nChat scraping is now an immediate operational priority.\n\nThe Framework has accumulated important decisions and corrections across