ished_duration_sec": 8, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "c94410e1-572e-4bb1-9614-e2b4a01a6610", "reasoning_end_time": 1789413096.7428806, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1789413088.514219, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "dfaf834e-87c4-4ab9-b6a0-37f7685e467a", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "8283cc73-6491-4e40-ad1c-100c69b0eaa5", "turn_id": "c34d9439-ad4d-4536-a635-4c1c2d6189a1", "working_turn_id": "8283cc73-6491-4e40-ad1c-100c69b0eaa5"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["We can pivot to Bedrock, but one important correction first: **Amazon Bedrock does not currently list a “DeepSeek V4 Flash” model.** The DeepSeek models AWS documents as available are **DeepSeek V3.2, DeepSeek V3.1, and DeepSeek-R1**. citeturn449027search3turn449027search11\n\nFor Talon through OpenCode, the cleanest Bedrock target is probably **DeepSeek V3.2 or V3.1 via Bedrock’s OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions path**, because AWS explicitly marks both as supporting Chat Completions. citeturn449027search1\n\nThe immediate path I’d use is:\n\n1. **Confirm your AWS region.** DeepSeek V3.2 is available in several regions including `us-east-1`, `us-east-2`, and `us-west-2`. citeturn449027search5\n2. **Confirm which DeepSeek model is actually enabled in your Bedrock account.**\n3. Point OpenCode at Bedrock rather than the DeepSeek direct provider.\n4. Test the provider with a trivial prompt **before loading Talon/bootstrap**.\n5. Once raw inference works, then load Talon from the correct identity path.\n\nAWS now exposes both the native `bedrock-runtime` endpoint and an OpenAI-compatible interface. For new applications, AWS recommends `bedrock-runtime`, and DeepSeek V3.1/V3.2 support the relevant APIs there. citeturn449027search6turn449027search1\n\nIf you want to verify from PowerShell first, run:\n\n```powershell\naws sts get-caller-identity\naws configure get region\naws bedrock list-foundation-models --region us-east-1 --query \"modelSummaries[?contains(modelId, 'deepseek')].[modelName,modelId]\" --output table\n```\n\nReplace `us-east-1` with your configured Bedrock region if different. AWS documents `ListFoundationModels` as the runtime-side way to enumerate Bedrock models. citeturn449027search9\n\nFor reference, AWS currently documents this Bedrock-native ID for **DeepSeek V3.1**:\n\n```text\ndeepseek.v3-v1:0\n```\n\non `bedrock-runtime`; AWS also exposes V3.1 through the newer mantle/OpenAI-compatible endpoint as `deepseek.v3.1`. citeturn449027search0\n\nDo **not** change Talon yet. First give me the output of those three commands, especially the DeepSeek model list. Then I can tell you exactly what to put into OpenCode so we are wiring the provider once instead of guessing at model names."]}, "create_time": 1789413092.475309, "end_turn": true, "id": "b5770949-bf29-4d2c-9bf8-c83121fc7368", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "dznpx7", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "m41i8i", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [{"alt": "([AWS Documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-cards-deepseek.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 278, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "AWS Documentation", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": null, "refs": [{"ref_index": 3, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}, {"ref_index": 11, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}], "snippet": "", "supporting_websites"