9-8581-43ae-8e2b-3886305d23e6"]}, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "07f7792d-3feb-4806-9111-4a13a5ec28e9", "reasoning_start_time": 1789413263.0215647, "reasoning_status": "is_reasoning", "request_id": "0370e162-0f31-428a-ae97-5b1539d88454", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "skip_reasoning_title": "Skip", "thinking_effort": "standard", "tool_icons": ["https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=docs.aws.amazon.com&sz=128"], "tool_summary_type": "web", "turn_exchange_id": "9f3962d5-f89d-47fa-949c-100dc2f4c39d", "turn_id": "dc8f2994-9297-4a5f-8df7-736c2d8b2647", "working_turn_id": "9f3962d5-f89d-47fa-949c-100dc2f4c39d"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content": "Worked for 4s", "content_type": "reasoning_recap"}, "create_time": 1789413267.809391, "end_turn": false, "id": "19943df1-9448-441a-9c1a-9f539ac27791", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finished_duration_sec": 4, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "597dcc16-5dd5-4f49-8406-0a785ed2af3e", "reasoning_end_time": 1789413267.795948, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1789413263.0215647, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "0370e162-0f31-428a-ae97-5b1539d88454", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "9f3962d5-f89d-47fa-949c-100dc2f4c39d", "turn_id": "dc8f2994-9297-4a5f-8df7-736c2d8b2647", "working_turn_id": "9f3962d5-f89d-47fa-949c-100dc2f4c39d"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Good — now we’ve hit a **real Bedrock-side restriction**, not a PowerShell problem.\n\nThe interesting part is that AWS’s current documentation says **DeepSeek V3.2 supports Converse** and is available in `us-east-2`, so `ValidationException: Operation not allowed` usually points to one of two things: either **account/model access is not actually enabled for invocation in that region**, or there is an **IAM/service-policy restriction** even though model discovery works. AWS notes that Converse ultimately requires `bedrock:InvokeModel`. citeturn529571search0turn529571search2turn529571search3\n\nLet’s isolate that with the smallest next test: use **InvokeModel** instead of Converse. AWS documents DeepSeek V3.2 on `bedrock-runtime` with model ID `deepseek.v3.2`, and provides an InvokeModel example for exactly this model. citeturn529571search1\n\nCreate a BOM-free request body:\n\n```powershell\n$body = @'\n{\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"Reply exactly: BEDROCK DEEPSEEK OK\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"max_tokens\": 128\n}\n'@\n\n[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText(\n  \"$env:TEMP\\deepseek-body.json\",\n  $body,\n  (New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false))\n)\n```\n\nThen run:\n\n```powershell\naws bedrock-runtime invoke-model `\n  --region us-east-2 `\n  --model-id deepseek.v3.2 `\n  --content-type application/json `\n  --accept application/json `\n  --body \"fileb://$env:TEMP\\deepseek-body.json\" `\n  \"$env:TEMP\\deepseek-response.json\"\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```powershell\nGet-Content \"$env:TEMP\\deepseek-response.json\"\n```\n\nThis gives us a clean fork:\n\n- **If InvokeModel works:** your Bedrock access is valid and the issue is specifically the Converse path. We can still wire OpenCode using a supported Bedrock/OpenAI-compatible route.\n- **If InvokeModel also says `Operation not allowed`:** then this is an account/access-policy problem, not Talon and not OpenCode.\n\nOne more important thing: model listing only proves the model is **catalog-visible**, not necessarily that your IAM principal can invoke it. So this test will settle that cleanly. citeturn529571search3"]}, "create_time": 1789413266.624883, "end_turn": true, "id": "a3c0ed53-c1b1-4a20-ae94-f57722b3ed31", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "3rsoee", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "q90t7e", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "eoqotb", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [{"alt": "([AWS Documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/models-api-compatibility.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 600, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "AWS Documentation", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": null, "refs": [{"ref_index": 0, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}, {"ref_index": 2, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}, {"ref_index": 3, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}], "snippet": "", "supporting_websites": [{"attribution": "AWS Documentation", "pub_date": null, "snippet": "", "title": "Regional availability by models - Amazon Bedrock", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/models-region-compatibility.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}, {"attribution": "AWS Documentation", "pub_date": null, "snippet": "", "title": "Converse - Amazon Bedrock", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_runtime_Converse.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "title": "API compatibility - Amazon Bedrock", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/models-api-compatibility.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "matched_text": "citeturn529571search0turn529571search2turn529571search3", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "